              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the Eighth Amendment requires a sentencing jury to consider mitigation factors related to the defendant's background, character, or the circumstances of the offense."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "84fa31bdeb4b0806425f8847b3ee400c702ce5ab9af370f0a6611b6609901679",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-84fa31bdeb4b-0000-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 12,
                "start": 12
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioner contends that Oregon's Supreme Court has broadly construed \"circumstances of the offense\" to include any evidence inconsistent with guilt, such as alibi evidence, a construction that is not constitutionally required."
        }
      ],
